# ...except the debug key. It must be committed, not generated: Android's default debug keystore is
# created per machine, so every CI runner would otherwise sign with a different key and each build
# would refuse to install over the previous one. A debug key is not a secret — password and alias
# are the Android defaults. The release keystore above stays ignored.
!app/debug.keystore
